     <h2>Form 210 is filed even when it means a refund</h2>
     <p>After the sale, the seller files form 210 for the result, gain or loss, within the three months that begin once a month has passed since the sale (Order EHA/3316/2010, article 5.a, as currently worded, which refers to article 14.4 of the Regulation). After paying the withholding, the buyer must give you the seller’s copy of Form 211. Enter its receipt number on Form 210 and claim the withholding attributable to your share of the sale. If it exceeds the tax due, you can request a refund of the difference, subject to the Tax Agency’s checks (Regulation, article 14.4). Without form 210 there is no refund. The other deadlines for the form are in our guide to <a href="modelo-210-non-resident-tax-spain.html">form 210 for non-residents</a>.</p>
 
